    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "For Sale by Private Treaty.\r\n\r\nDennehy Auctioneers are delighted to offer this charming timber constructed summer chalet with a plastered exterior, superbly positioned in a highly desirable coastal setting close to Myrtleville Beach.\r\nThe property presents an exciting opportunity for purchasers seeking a renovation project, with excellent potential to refurbish and transform the existing chalet into a comfortable permanent residence or an idyllic coastal retreat, subject to any necessary planning requirements. (This property would not qualify for a standard mortgage due to its construction and condition.)\r\nEnjoying attractive views across Cork’s Outer Harbour and located just a short stroll from the beautiful Myrtleville Beach, this unique property combines considerable potential with an enviable seaside location. An increasingly rare opportunity to create a truly special home in one of Cork Harbour’s most sought after coastal settings.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises of Sitting Room, Kitchen, Three Bedrooms and Shower Room.\r\n\r\nComposite PVC door to kitchen.\r\n\r\nKitchen: 1.7 m  x 3.8 m\r\nShower room off. Door to sitting room.\r\n\r\nSitting Room: 2.37 m x 3.8 m \r\nTwo Bedrooms off and additional sitting room or possibly conversion to a large bedroom.\r\n\r\nAdditional Sitting Room/Large Bedroom: 4.46 m x 2.3 m\r\nDelightful views over Corks outer harbour.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two: 2 m x 2.11 m\r\n\r\nBedroom Three: 1.65 m x 2 m\r\n\r\nShower Room/W.C:\r\nOff Kitchen in a dilapidated condition.\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\nGood sized lawn, decking area, side lawn. Gardens are partially walled in with concrete block wall and mature hedging. Small Steel Tech shed in rear garden.\r\n\r\nServices:\r\nMains water, mains electricity, septic tank."
      },
      {
